  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As show in the figure, in steady state, the charge stored in the capacitor is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0060_a04af0351cf5.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 185px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>At the steady state, there will be no current through the capacitor. Therefore, potential difference across capacitor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Charge on capacitor is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}